{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993367511352001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bogus-spray-scat","assignee":"","author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":5},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782667990086772001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6d53fb85-d513-4dbd-876b-b6aa0d122e39","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a42b-362a-937e-4fc1"}],"description":"The plan-review gate's **Pass-2 verifier returns an empty `verifications` list**, so every Pass-1 finding reaches `pass3_decide` with no verification → `decision: indeterminate, reason: \"no-verification\"`. When ALL findings are no-verification (zero resolved), the verdict is forced INDETERMINATE, which is NOT signable → the plan-review claim gate blocks the ticket. This blocked epic 5ca8's children (clay-cake-act: 0 blocking, deterministic floor all PASS, 4 findings all no-verification → INDETERMINATE across multiple plan-hardening passes). It affects ANY `mode=\"structured\"` prompted LLM op (the same json-repair path).\n\n## Root cause (proven via joe-debug, runtime evidence)\nThe structured-output reliability stack (story 1268) has two paths in `_pai_structured` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py`): a NATIVE path (`Agent(model, output_type=mode_obj)` — schema enforced) and an Anthropic PROMPTED path that generates FREE TEXT then tolerantly parses (json-repair). `structured.output_mode` returns `PromptedOutput(model_cls)` for Anthropic (which would inject the schema into the prompt), BUT the prompted branch built `Agent(model, **kwargs)` with `output_type=str` and **discarded `mode_obj`** — so the JSON schema was NEVER conveyed to the model. The model, knowing fields only from the verifier prompt's PROSE (\"severity ATTRIBUTES\", \"BINARY sub-answers\"), emitted plausible-but-divergent keys — captured live:\n\n```\n{\"findings\": [{\"index\": 0, \"attributes\": {...}, \"sub_answers\": {...}}]}\n```\n\ninstead of the `plan_review_verification` contract shape `{\"verifications\": [{\"index\", \"severity_attributes\", \"binary\"}]}`. `VerificationOutput` ignores unknown keys, so tolerant parsing produced `VerificationOutput(verifications=[])` — a VALID, EMPTY object, no error raised. Instrumented run: `verify-step … verifs_per_chunk=[0] merged_verifs=0` → `decide: findings=4 raw_verifs=0` → all 4 no-verification.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS=50 rebar review-plan <a-task-with-code-grounded-findings> -o json`.\n2. Inspect `indeterminate` findings — all carry `reason: \"no-verification\"`; `blocking`/`advisory` empty; verdict INDETERMINATE despite the deterministic floor passing.\n\n- **Expected:** the verifier emits schema-conforming `verifications` (keyed by 0-based `index`); `pass3_decide` resolves each finding to advisory/dropped; the verdict reaches PASS/BLOCK.\n- **Actual:** the verifier emits a divergent JSON shape (schema never conveyed) → empty `verifications` → all findings no-verification → INDETERMINATE.\n\n## Fix\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured.py`: add `schema_directive(model_cls)` rendering the model's JSON Schema with a \"use these EXACT keys; JSON only\" directive.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` `_pai_structured` PROMPTED path: append `schema_directive(model_cls)` to the initial prompt AND the bounded-retry prompt, so the model is told the exact output shape (restoring the schema-conveyance that `PromptedOutput` provides and the json-repair refactor dropped). NativeOutput path unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The prompted structured path conveys the output JSON schema to the model (a unit test with a schema-aware FunctionModel proves a `mode=\"structured\"` run yields non-empty, correctly-keyed structured output only because the schema reached the prompt; mutation-checked).\n- [ ] A real `rebar review-plan` on a task with code-grounded findings produces resolved verifications (findings become advisory/dropped, NOT a wholesale no-verification set) and the verdict is no longer forced INDETERMINATE by empty verifications.\n- [ ] No regression: the runner-hardening / structured / pydantic-ai runner suites pass; `make check` clean.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a9bb8cf7-0550-466f-a8c6-9f536b69e771","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2f18-9294-7be8-4eff","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Plan-review verifier returns empty verifications (schema not conveyed in prompted structured path)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3646e47f-a544-4ecf-9970-6eea7abad466","6d53fb85-d513-4dbd-876b-b6aa0d122e39","a9bb8cf7-0550-466f-a8c6-9f536b69e771","c0a606cf-a206-4a36-bc7e-b42ddf2ca2b6","055c0607-dbb2-4b3e-afe5-2e18c50bb18f"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993367511352001,"uuid":"1b10c180-d38e-46cf-b720-95c496a736bf"}